From 33f4833037aa7de3e81eded09ee91d0a78d9df02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilja Livenson <ilja.livenson@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:36:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] auth: show users only their own jobs in partitions, node
 process samples and named queries

Any authenticated user got every user's jobs from routes outside the
job routes: the pending and running jobs of each partition, the
per-process GPU samples of a node (timeseries by job, and the latest
utilization with its pids), and the rows of the user-job-results,
user-success-job-results, user-failed-job-results and
jobs-exceeding-resource-usage queries. Like the job routes, these now
give a user without the admin realm role only their own jobs, and the
named queries answer 403. The queries' check is a dependency, so it
runs before the route's URL-keyed response cache.

NoneForUserWithRealmRoles reads whether OAuth is required when called
instead of when the route is defined, like get_token_payload.

The node process GPU timeseries also returned only the last job of each
GPU: a GPU's list was reset for every process.

The test data gets jobs of two users (TestDBConfig.user_names), and the
endpoint smoke test uses an admin token, since the job routes now scope
to the token's user in tests too.
